    "narrative": "Our offensive outlook for today is headlined by **Bryce Harper** (78.15) and **Taylor Ward** (71.19), who emerge as our premier starters. **Bryce Harper** sits atop our projections, benefiting from a soft matchup against Brady Singer and an assumed leadoff spot that maximizes his plate appearances and run-scoring potential. Meanwhile, **Taylor Ward** offers an exceptional blend of park factors and platoon advantage against David Peterson, making him a locked-in asset despite the lower-tier opponent xERA. We are also monitoring **Luis Arraez** (69.53) and **Zack Gelof** (67.85) closely; the wind conditions are providing a tangible boost to **Luis Arraez**, while **Zack Gelof** remains a priority start due to his stolen base upside against a slower pitcher, which is vital for our scarcity-driven strategy.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **JJ Bleday** (51.32), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Drew Gilbert** and **Jonathan Aranda**. While **JJ Bleday** received a significant boost from his platoon edge, the underlying SP skill of his opponent suppressed his efficiency score just enough to keep him on the bench in favor of players with more favorable game environments. We remain cautious regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for most of our squad; until official cards are turned in, we are projecting lineups based on historical trends. Notably, **Lawrence Butler** is carrying a slightly lower score of 56.10 due to a negative platoon split against Framber Valdez, but he retains his spot as we look to balance our daily caps. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** still sidelined on the IL, our depth is being tested, but the current configuration positions us well to chase efficiency in the 5x5 categories.",
